+## Turn usage
+
+`afterModelResponse` is the hook a deployer reaches for to record what a turn cost, so the `usage` it receives covers every provider call the turn made, not only the last. A turn that ran no tools makes one provider call, so it reports exactly what that call reported.
+
+- A turn driven through two tool rounds hands `afterModelResponse` the field-by-field sum of the usage every provider call in that turn reported ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call in a turn driven through two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L63)).
+- A round whose provider reports no usage adds nothing, so the rounds that did report are still counted, and a turn in which no round reported hands the hook `undefined` rather than zeros or `NaN` ([validated by: counts the rounds that reported usage when others did not, and reports nothing when none did](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L73)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
